// Five-Card Stud — the formal casino form, fixed limit, three-handed.
//
// Rules source: Pagat, https://www.pagat.com/poker/variants/5stud.html, fetched
// live 2026-09-06. Each player antes; one card down and one up; four betting
// rounds; the third, fourth and fifth cards are all dealt face up. Showdown is
// the best five-card poker hand among the players still in, or the last player
// standing takes the pot. Pagat's page supports up to ten players; three is
// this file's table.
//
// THE VARIANT. Pagat's base text is the traditional home game, and marks the
// casino rules as departures from it. This file is the casino form throughout,
// which is one choice made once — the three places the page names it are
// consistent with each other and are quoted at the rules they govern below:
// the compulsory bring-in opens the first round, the last two rounds are big
// bets only, and every wager on a street is that street's size.
//
// The .cardlang runtime needs a terminal, so as in the corpus's Seven-Card Stud
// this plays a session until one player holds all the chips and declares that
// player the winner. Pagat's page describes a cash game with no overall winner.
//
// CHIP UNIT. One unit = $0.50, which makes Pagat's whole $0.50/$2/$5/$10 ladder
// exact in the Integer chips the language gives: ante 1, bring-in 4, small bet
// 10, big bet 20. Nothing is rounded.
//
// LIMIT LADDER.
//   Round 1 (two cards): small bet. "In the first betting round no big bets are
//     allowed."
//   Round 2 (three cards): "big bets ($10) are allowed if any player has a pair
//     (or better) showing." The page adds "In this case anyone can place a big
//     bet or raise, even if they do not themselves have a pair", which is why
//     the condition sizes the STREET rather than one seat's move. See the
//     second deviation below for the half of that sentence the file cannot say.
//   Rounds 3 and 4 (four and five cards): big bet. "Some play that in the last
//     two betting rounds, after players are dealt their fourth and fifth cards,
//     only big bets are allowed. This is the normal rule in casino hosted
//     games, but not in home poker games."
// Once a big bet is placed, the raises answering it are big too, which is the
// casino arm of the page's note that "if the rule is played that each raise
// must be at least as large as the last bet or raise, then after a player
// places a big bet, only big raises are allowed in that round" — the home rule
// it offers instead lets a small raise answer a big bet.
//
// WHO OPENS. Round 1 is opened by the compulsory bring-in: "Some play that the
// first betting round starts with a compulsory (bring-in) bet by the player
// showing the lowest card. This is now the normal rule in formal games hosted
// by American casinos." Rounds 2 to 4 are opened by the best hand showing —
// "pairs, triplets, two pairs and quads count in their normal poker order - so
// for example with three cards showing 3-3-3 is higher than 7-7-8, which is
// higher than A-K-Q. Incomplete straights and flushes do not count" — with ties
// broken on the suit of the highest card. That order is `best_showing_seat`.
//
// RAISE CAP. "Only one bet and a maximum of three raises are allowed in any
// betting round, if there were more than two active players at the start of the
// betting round." The trailing clause is a real rule, so `raise_cap` is set per
// street from the count of seats that can act rather than declared once. The
// bring-in is short of a full bet and so spends none of the cap: "A bring-in of
// less than a small bet does not count as a bet for this purpose - after it is
// completed there can be three raises."
//
// DEVIATIONS. Two, and both are rules the language cannot yet state. Every
// other rule above is in the file as itself.
//
// FIRST: the heads-up arm of the raise cap is UNCAPPED, and there is no way to
// say so (issue #635, which this game is the witness for). `raise_cap` is an
// Integer, so "no cap" is written as a bound the street cannot reach — see the
// first street's comment for the derivation. The betting behaves identically,
// but a reader meets a magic number where the rule says "unlimited", and a
// variant with deeper stacks would need the number recomputed.
//
// SECOND: on the open-pair street the big bet is ALLOWED, not compulsory —
// "anyone can place a big bet or raise" — so both sizes are legal there and a
// seat may still open for the small bet. A street opens at ONE size
// (`open_street` sets `limit`, which the library owns and the game may not
// write), so the conditional below makes the big bet the street's only size
// where the rules make it the street's second one. A seat that would bet 10
// into an open pair cannot. That is issue #648, which this game also witnesses,
// and it is the same shortfall #546 records against Seven-Card Stud from the
// other side: that file never offers the big bet, this one never offers the
// small.
//
// NO BURN CARD. Pagat's five-card-stud page does not burn between streets, so
// this file does not.
//
// NO DEALER BUTTON. Nothing in Five-Card Stud reads one: every street's opener
// is chosen from the up cards, and the deck is shuffled whole each hand, so a
// rotating deal order would change no distribution and no decision.
//
// The fifth card is dealt FACE UP, which is the page's base text; dealing it
// face down is one of the page's Variations and is not this file's game.

game FiveCardStud {

  // check / bet / call / raise and the ring predicates come from the family
  // library the corpus's poker games share (docs/libraries/poker_betting.cardlang).
  // `fold` is this game's own, at the foot of the file: where a folder's cards
  // go is a fact about these zones, not about betting.
  uses poker_betting

  players: 3
  direction: clockwise
  max_length: 30000

  cards: standard52
  ranking: aces high

  // The two seat selectors and the side-pot settlement, declared with what each
  // reads. `committed`, `folded` and `in_hand` are declared by `phase play`, so
  // a read of one names that phase; `stack` is game-level and carries no tail.
  primitives {
    bring_in_seat() : Player
        reads stack, upcards
    best_showing_seat() : Player
        reads folded in play, upcards
    pot_share(p : Player) : Integer
        reads committed in play, folded in play, in_hand in play, hole, upcards
  }

  zones {
    deck            : Deck
    hole[player]    : Hand<player>           // the one face-down card
    upcards[player] : PublicHand<player>     // the four face-up cards
    muck            : Muck                   // folded and spent cards
  }

  state {
    stack[player] : Integer = 200            // $100 at one unit = $0.50
  }

  phase hand_sequence repeat until (number of players where stack[player] > 0) <= 1 {

    before_each {
      move all cards to deck
      shuffle deck
    }

    phase play {
      state {
        in_hand[player]   : Boolean = false   // entered the hand holding chips
        committed[player] : Integer = 0       // chips put in this hand (side pots)
        folded[player]    : Boolean = false
        bet_by[player]    : Integer = 0       // chips put in on the current street
        bet_to_match      : Integer = 0       // the street's standing bet
        level             : Integer = 0       // the last FULL wager this street
        raises            : Integer = 0       // aggressions so far this street
        raise_cap         : Integer = 4       // set per street, below
      }

      // The entrants: everyone holding a chip. Ante and deal follow this set.
      for each player p: in_hand[p] := stack[p] > 0
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        stack[p] := stack[p] - 1
        committed[p] := committed[p] + 1
      }

      // One down, one up.
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        deal 1 card from deck to hole[p]
        deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p]
      }

      // FIRST BETTING ROUND — bring-in by the lowest card showing, small bet.
      // Skipped only when fewer than two entrants can act (everyone all-in on
      // the ante), in which case the hand runs straight to the showdown.
      if (number of players where stack[player] > 0) >= 2 {
        run open_street(10)
        // Uncapped heads-up. The language takes an Integer, so "no cap" is a
        // number no street can reach. A counted aggression lifts `level` by at
        // least half the street's limit (`raise`'s half-bet arm), the smallest
        // limit here is 10, and no seat can put more than the table's 600 chips
        // into one street: at most 600/5 counted aggressions, so 120 stands in
        // for "unlimited". Deeper stacks would need it recomputed (issue #635).
        raise_cap := if (number of players where can_act(player)) > 2 then 4 else 120
        let bringer = bring_in_seat()
        // A forced post, not a decision: the lowest card puts in 4 (all-in if
        // it holds less) and that stands as the opening bet. It is short of a
        // full bet, so `level` stays 0 and the next wager COMPLETES to 10
        // rather than raising to 14.
        bet_by[bringer] := if 4 < stack[bringer] then 4 else stack[bringer]
        stack[bringer] := stack[bringer] - bet_by[bringer]
        committed[bringer] := committed[bringer] + bet_by[bringer]
        bet_to_match := 4
        // The ring opens ON the poster, because the poster holds the round's
        // first decision: "The player who opens the betting has the option to
        // place a full small bet ($5) instead of just the compulsory minimum
        // $2." The post is made, so the poster owes nothing and `check` is the
        // move that stands on the minimum; `raise` is the option, and it
        // completes to the street's size rather than adding one to the post.
        // Which of the two the poster takes is what the seats behind it then
        // face: "If the opener just places the minimum bring-in, subsequent
        // players have the option to complete the bet to a small bet ($5), to
        // call the bring-in ($2) or to fold. Only if someone completes the bet
        // are later players allowed to raise. If the opener chooses to begin
        // with a full bet ($5), subsequent players can raise."
        round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from bringer
              over players where pending(player)
              until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                 or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                     and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
      }

      // SECOND BETTING ROUND — third card face up. Small bet, or the big bet if
      // any player shows a pair or better. A folder's up cards are already in
      // the muck, so `shows_pair` cannot see them. The rules leave BOTH sizes
      // legal when a pair shows and a street carries one; the header's second
      // deviation and issue #648 hold what that costs.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(if (number of players where shows_pair(player)) > 0 then 20 else 10)
          raise_cap := if (number of players where can_act(player)) > 2 then 4 else 120
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // THIRD BETTING ROUND — fourth card face up, big bet.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(20)
          raise_cap := if (number of players where can_act(player)) > 2 then 4 else 120
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // FOURTH BETTING ROUND — fifth card face up, big bet.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] { deal 1 card from deck to upcards[p] }
        if (number of players where can_act(player)) >= 2 {
          run open_street(20)
          raise_cap := if (number of players where can_act(player)) > 2 then 4 else 120
          round offering [check, bet, call, fold, raise] from best_showing_seat()
                over players where pending(player)
                until (number of players where pending(player)) is 0
                   or ((number of players where can_act(player)) <= 1
                       and (number of players where can_act(player) and owes(player)) is 0)
        }
      }

      // SHOWDOWN. A contested hand turns the hole card up before the pot is
      // judged; a lone contender collects without showing. Each entrant then
      // takes its side-pot share and the hands leave play to the muck.
      if (number of players where in_hand[player] and not folded[player]) > 1 {
        for each player p: if in_hand[p] and not folded[p] {
          move all cards from hole[p] to upcards[p]
        }
      }
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        stack[p] := stack[p] + pot_share(p)
      }
      for each player p: if in_hand[p] {
        move all cards from hole[p] to muck
        move all cards from upcards[p] to muck
      }
    }
  }

  winner: highest stack
}

// Five-Card Stud's own betting move. The folder's up cards go straight to the
// muck, so opponents stop seeing them and their information sets carry that;
// the hole card stays face down until the end-of-hand cleanup. Offered
// alongside the four imported moves in one vocabulary list, and the `when:`
// guards filter to the exact option list per decision.
move_type fold {
  when: bet_to_match > bet_by[actor]
  effect {
    folded[actor] := true
    move all cards from upcards[actor] to muck
  }
}

// Does this seat show a pair or better among its face-up cards? Two face-up
// cards of a rank is a pair showing; three is trips, which is "or better" and
// the same test. Factored as a function so the rank binder does not nest
// inside the player binder.
function up_rank_count(p : Player, r : Rank) = number of cards in upcards[p] where card.rank is r
function shows_pair(p : Player) = any rank where up_rank_count(p, rank) >= 2
